# LADE — ignored paths.
#
# Profiles are symlinked into ~/.hermes/profiles/, so Hermes writes its runtime
# state directly inside these directories: state.db, memories, sessions, cache,
# logs, backups, locks, gateway and plugin metadata, and — on first run — a copy
# of its bundled skills. None of that is source.
#
# Kept in git under profiles/<role>/: AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, profile.yaml,
# config.yaml. The skills/ directory is generated by setup.sh from the role
# manifest and is ignored: the manifest is the source of truth.

# Everything under profiles/<role>/, then the four source files back in.
profiles/*/*
!profiles/*/AGENTS.md
!profiles/*/SOUL.md
!profiles/*/profile.yaml
!profiles/*/config.yaml

# Local tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.DS_Store
# Makefile: local archives and compiled helpers
.lade-backups/

# Task instances and artifacts are produced at run time, never committed here.
task.md
